        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Multiplication Table</h3>
        <p>Yesterday you saw how nested loops create grids. Today you'll build something useful: a multiplication table that displays all products from 1×1 through 12×12.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>MultiplicationTable</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Use nested for loops: outer loop for rows (1 to 12), inner loop for columns (1 to 12).</li>
            <li>Print each product aligned in columns. Use <code>System.out.printf("%4d", row * col)</code> for alignment.</li>
            <li>After each inner loop, print a newline to start the next row.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Observe</h3>
        <p>Which executes more often — the outer loop body or the inner loop body? Count the total number of print statements. If you swapped the loop variables (i becomes column, j becomes row), would the table look different?</p>
    </div>
</div>

